1
00:00:01,058 --> 00:00:04,600
On day 241, the driver comes to the radio.

2
00:00:04,600 --> 00:00:05,888
Nobody has slept much.

3
00:00:05,888 --> 00:00:07,455
The radio sits on the bench

4
00:00:07,455 --> 00:00:08,753
between the four of you,

5
00:00:08,753 --> 00:00:11,152
quiet now, as if it is waiting too.

6
00:00:11,638 --> 00:00:13,001
Vera has not let go of

7
00:00:13,001 --> 00:00:14,364
her goggles all night.

8
00:00:14,364 --> 00:00:15,849
Your name is Patch.

9
00:00:16,367 --> 00:00:17,398
Two hundred and forty days ago,

10
00:00:17,398 --> 00:00:19,761
you were waiting for a bus.

11
00:00:20,166 --> 00:00:22,146
Since then, you have lived under a

12
00:00:22,146 --> 00:00:24,640
bus depot with Nora, who used to clean it,

13
00:00:24,640 --> 00:00:26,547
Wes, who used to live on a roof,

14
00:00:26,547 --> 00:00:29,028
and Vera, who drove the last bus out of

15
00:00:29,028 --> 00:00:31,219
your yard with the whole horde behind her.

16
00:00:31,219 --> 00:00:32,272
Your yard is empty.

17
00:00:32,272 --> 00:00:33,482
Your gate is your own.

18
00:00:33,482 --> 00:00:35,207
And at the end of the motorway,

19
00:00:35,207 --> 00:00:39,258
a few thousand of the dead are standing on somebody else's bridge,

20
00:00:39,258 --> 00:00:40,633
because you put them there.

21
00:00:40,633 --> 00:00:42,620
At sunset, the radio crackles.

22
00:00:42,620 --> 00:00:45,425
Vera picks it up before anybody else can.

23
00:00:45,425 --> 00:00:47,735
"This is the driver," she says.

24
00:00:47,735 --> 00:00:48,748
A pause.

25
00:00:49,203 --> 00:00:51,503
Then the same careful, tired voice.

26
00:00:51,503 --> 00:00:54,199
"Thank you for coming to the radio.

27
00:00:54,199 --> 00:00:55,282
My name is Ansel.

28
00:00:55,282 --> 00:00:57,283
Before you say anything,

29
00:00:57,283 --> 00:00:59,193
nobody here is angry."

30
00:00:59,193 --> 00:01:00,496
Another pause.

31
00:01:00,496 --> 00:01:01,317
"Well.

32
00:01:01,642 --> 00:01:02,737
Some of us were.

33
00:01:02,737 --> 00:01:03,896
For about a week."

34
00:01:03,896 --> 00:01:05,419
Vera says nothing.

35
00:01:05,792 --> 00:01:07,711
Her thumb moves over the button.

36
00:01:07,711 --> 00:01:10,363
"That bridge is the only road from our

37
00:01:10,363 --> 00:01:11,555
streets to our fields,

38
00:01:11,555 --> 00:01:15,161
and to the spring where we get our water," says Ansel.

39
00:01:15,161 --> 00:01:16,847
"For a month,

40
00:01:16,847 --> 00:01:20,277
we've been walking under a few thousand of them to fetch it.

41
00:01:20,277 --> 00:01:21,364
Very quietly.

42
00:01:21,963 --> 00:01:24,149
We'd like to stop being quiet."

43
00:01:24,149 --> 00:01:26,529
"So would everybody," says Vera.

44
00:01:26,529 --> 00:01:28,991
"We watched you move them," he says.

45
00:01:29,349 --> 00:01:30,439
"We have diesel.

46
00:01:30,439 --> 00:01:32,209
And nobody here can drive

47
00:01:32,209 --> 00:01:35,841
anything bigger than a wheelbarrow."

48
00:01:35,841 --> 00:01:38,787
From day 242 to day 244,

49
00:01:38,787 --> 00:01:41,435
the depot talks about it.

50
00:01:41,809 --> 00:01:42,870
Not in whispers.

51
00:01:42,870 --> 00:01:44,855
You don't whisper anymore.

52
00:01:45,390 --> 00:01:46,940
But it is the kind of talking

53
00:01:46,940 --> 00:01:48,935
that goes around in circles,

54
00:01:48,935 --> 00:01:50,520
round and round the bench,

55
00:01:50,520 --> 00:01:53,626
the way the river used to go around the yard.

56
00:01:53,626 --> 00:01:57,010
"We could say no," says Wes, on day 242.

57
00:01:57,010 --> 00:01:59,775
"We only just got the yard."

58
00:02:00,341 --> 00:02:01,930
Nobody answers him.

59
00:02:01,930 --> 00:02:03,042
Not even Wes.

60
00:02:03,042 --> 00:02:05,145
He goes up and oils the gate,

61
00:02:05,145 --> 00:02:07,022
although he oiled it yesterday,

62
00:02:07,022 --> 00:02:09,261
and comes back down and sits on the bench,

63
00:02:09,261 --> 00:02:11,939
and looks at the jump leads hanging on their hook.

64
00:02:11,939 --> 00:02:13,443
"I'm just saying it out

65
00:02:13,443 --> 00:02:17,497
loud," he says, "so it's been said."

66
00:02:17,497 --> 00:02:20,789
On day 243, Nora stands in front of the

67
00:02:20,789 --> 00:02:23,430
chart on the bunker wall for a long time.

68
00:02:23,430 --> 00:02:23,950
Days.

69
00:02:23,950 --> 00:02:25,162
Zombies gone.

70
00:02:25,162 --> 00:02:26,715
People met.

71
00:02:26,715 --> 00:02:27,803
Days in daylight.

72
00:02:27,803 --> 00:02:30,460
She puts her finger on the third column.

73
00:02:30,801 --> 00:02:32,687
"We know what it's like," she says.

74
00:02:32,687 --> 00:02:34,595
"Having them on your ceiling."

75
00:02:35,673 --> 00:02:38,223
On day 244, Vera asks you the

76
00:02:38,223 --> 00:02:40,763
question nobody has asked yet.

77
00:02:40,763 --> 00:02:42,065
"What's the rule?"

78
00:02:42,065 --> 00:02:44,357
"If they come toward the gate,

79
00:02:44,357 --> 00:02:45,435
you close it," you say.

80
00:02:45,435 --> 00:02:47,094
"Even if somebody is outside."

81
00:02:47,497 --> 00:02:49,859
"And if you're the one who sent them?"

82
00:02:49,859 --> 00:02:52,234
You have kept that rule for

83
00:02:52,234 --> 00:02:52,970
two hundred and forty days.

84
00:02:52,970 --> 00:02:56,309
It has never said anything about that.

85
00:02:56,309 --> 00:02:59,208
"Then we go and get them back," you say.

86
00:02:59,646 --> 00:03:00,829
Vera turns her goggles

87
00:03:00,829 --> 00:03:02,064
over once in her hands.

88
00:03:02,064 --> 00:03:03,599
Then she pulls them on.

89
00:03:04,118 --> 00:03:07,404
On day 245, the depot gets a new keeper.

90
00:03:07,827 --> 00:03:09,505
At midday, three people walk down

91
00:03:09,505 --> 00:03:11,707
the hill road with blue bandages.

92
00:03:12,066 --> 00:03:13,322
Two grown-ups and the boy

93
00:03:13,322 --> 00:03:14,736
who learned the horn code.

94
00:03:14,736 --> 00:03:16,895
They are going to keep the depot,

95
00:03:16,895 --> 00:03:18,772
because this time, Wes is coming.

96
00:03:19,548 --> 00:03:21,882
"Last time, I got the gate," he says.

97
00:03:21,882 --> 00:03:24,089
"This time, I want the motorway.

98
00:03:24,089 --> 00:03:25,111
I've never seen one with

99
00:03:25,111 --> 00:03:26,720
things on it that weren't dead."

100
00:03:27,239 --> 00:03:29,049
You show the boy the rope on the bolt,

101
00:03:29,049 --> 00:03:31,173
the canopy ladder and the gantry.

102
00:03:31,173 --> 00:03:32,782
He listens very seriously.

103
00:03:32,782 --> 00:03:34,869
Then Nora gives him the flashlight

104
00:03:34,869 --> 00:03:37,534
for the gate and shows him the knock.

105
00:03:37,534 --> 00:03:38,044
Three times.

106
00:03:38,044 --> 00:03:39,967
Then a fourth time, softer.

107
00:03:39,967 --> 00:03:42,044
"If somebody knocks any other

108
00:03:42,044 --> 00:03:44,761
way," she says, "you don't open."

109
00:03:44,761 --> 00:03:46,202
He nods as if he will

110
00:03:46,202 --> 00:03:49,087
remember it for the rest of his life.

111
00:03:49,087 --> 00:03:51,392
You drive out at dusk, four of you in a

112
00:03:51,392 --> 00:03:53,587
cab built for three, with the orange bag

113
00:03:53,587 --> 00:03:55,742
between your feet, and the sign over

114
00:03:55,742 --> 00:03:58,719
the street swinging in the wind behind you.

115
00:03:58,719 --> 00:03:59,864
FOUR ALIVE.

116
00:03:59,864 --> 00:04:01,771
For the first time,

117
00:04:01,771 --> 00:04:05,213
all four of them are on the wrong side of it.

118
00:04:05,213 --> 00:04:08,111
On day 246, you drive back to the coach.

119
00:04:08,111 --> 00:04:10,142
It sits exactly where Vera left it,

120
00:04:10,142 --> 00:04:11,462
alone in its lanes,

121
00:04:11,462 --> 00:04:14,178
beige and patient, with frost on the windows.

122
00:04:14,178 --> 00:04:16,115
Vera walks around it once and

123
00:04:16,115 --> 00:04:17,232
puts her hand on the side,

124
00:04:17,232 --> 00:04:19,295
the way the hill people patted the truck.

125
00:04:19,295 --> 00:04:22,346
Across the frozen field beside the motorway,

126
00:04:22,346 --> 00:04:23,141
three people are

127
00:04:23,141 --> 00:04:25,587
walking toward you, pulling a handcart.

128
00:04:25,587 --> 00:04:26,850
A woman, a girl,

129
00:04:26,850 --> 00:04:29,025
and a tall, thin man in a long coat,

130
00:04:29,025 --> 00:04:31,790
with one yellow mitten and one green one.

131
00:04:31,790 --> 00:04:34,449
He stops on the other side of the barrier,

132
00:04:34,449 --> 00:04:35,555
looks at the four of you,

133
00:04:35,555 --> 00:04:37,250
and then looks only at Vera.

134
00:04:37,896 --> 00:04:39,295
"Ansel," he says.

135
00:04:39,295 --> 00:04:41,257
"I know," says Vera.

136
00:04:41,823 --> 00:04:42,617
"You said."

137
00:04:42,617 --> 00:04:45,233
The handcart is full of fuel cans.

138
00:04:45,590 --> 00:04:47,269
Ansel lifts the first one over

139
00:04:47,269 --> 00:04:48,406
the barrier himself,

140
00:04:48,406 --> 00:04:51,202
and puts it down at Vera's feet like an apology,

141
00:04:51,202 --> 00:04:53,208
although it isn't his to make.

142
00:04:53,646 --> 00:04:55,393
"There was a light," Vera says.

143
00:04:55,393 --> 00:04:56,849
"On the edge of the city.

144
00:04:56,849 --> 00:04:57,848
One window."

145
00:04:58,431 --> 00:04:59,367
Ansel nods.

146
00:04:59,367 --> 00:05:00,381
"That was us.

147
00:05:00,381 --> 00:05:02,782
We saw you up on the roof of that bus,

148
00:05:02,782 --> 00:05:03,726
the first morning.

149
00:05:03,726 --> 00:05:05,496
We couldn't get to you.

150
00:05:05,496 --> 00:05:07,223
Not with all of them in the way.

151
00:05:07,223 --> 00:05:09,407
So we kept a lamp in the window every night,

152
00:05:09,407 --> 00:05:11,352
so you'd know somebody had seen you."

153
00:05:12,015 --> 00:05:14,004
Vera looks at him for a long time.

154
00:05:14,004 --> 00:05:15,084
"I thought you were

155
00:05:15,084 --> 00:05:16,770
very tidy dead," she says.

156
00:05:16,770 --> 00:05:19,658
"Some days," says Ansel, "we were close."

157
00:05:20,351 --> 00:05:23,813
From day 247 to day 249,

158
00:05:23,813 --> 00:05:25,752
the coach comes back to life.

159
00:05:25,752 --> 00:05:27,707
The diesel goes into the tank,

160
00:05:27,707 --> 00:05:30,729
can after can, with the girl holding the funnel.

161
00:05:30,729 --> 00:05:32,344
Wes climbs into the

162
00:05:32,344 --> 00:05:33,944
driver's seat and tries the key.

163
00:05:33,944 --> 00:05:35,959
The dashboard lights up, faintly.

164
00:05:35,959 --> 00:05:37,373
The starter turns once,

165
00:05:37,373 --> 00:05:40,213
slowly, like somebody waking up on a Monday.

166
00:05:40,213 --> 00:05:41,233
Then nothing.

167
00:05:41,233 --> 00:05:43,211
"It's been standing in the

168
00:05:43,211 --> 00:05:45,878
frost for two months," says Vera.

169
00:05:45,878 --> 00:05:47,383
"It's sulking."

170
00:05:48,012 --> 00:05:49,488
So you drive the white truck

171
00:05:49,488 --> 00:05:50,812
around to face the coach,

172
00:05:50,812 --> 00:05:54,246
nose to nose, and Wes takes out the jump leads.

173
00:05:54,246 --> 00:05:56,467
The same jump leads he has

174
00:05:56,467 --> 00:05:58,462
been looking at since day 206.

175
00:05:58,462 --> 00:05:59,375
Red to red.

176
00:05:59,375 --> 00:06:00,699
Black to black.

177
00:06:00,699 --> 00:06:02,568
He checks it three times,

178
00:06:02,568 --> 00:06:04,206
with hand movements.

179
00:06:04,206 --> 00:06:06,676
On day 248, Vera turns the key.

180
00:06:06,676 --> 00:06:07,965
The coach coughs.

181
00:06:07,965 --> 00:06:09,562
Coughs again.

182
00:06:09,562 --> 00:06:10,111
Catches.

183
00:06:10,111 --> 00:06:13,640
A deep diesel rumble rolls out over the motorway,

184
00:06:13,640 --> 00:06:14,858
and Vera sits back in the

185
00:06:14,858 --> 00:06:17,510
driver's seat with both hands on the big wheel,

186
00:06:17,510 --> 00:06:18,672
and closes her eyes,

187
00:06:18,672 --> 00:06:22,057
as if somebody has just played her favorite song.

188
00:06:22,057 --> 00:06:24,614
On day 249, you sit on the barrier

189
00:06:24,614 --> 00:06:26,350
with Ansel and his people,

190
00:06:26,350 --> 00:06:28,079
eating the bread they brought,

191
00:06:28,079 --> 00:06:31,070
and you ask him the only question that matters.

192
00:06:31,070 --> 00:06:32,533
"Where do we take them?"

193
00:06:32,987 --> 00:06:33,851
Not away.

194
00:06:33,851 --> 00:06:37,173
Away is just somebody else's door.

195
00:06:37,579 --> 00:06:38,939
You have learned that.

196
00:06:38,939 --> 00:06:40,299
Ansel thinks about it.

197
00:06:40,299 --> 00:06:42,140
Then he picks up a stick and

198
00:06:42,140 --> 00:06:44,242
draws in the frost on the road.

199
00:06:44,242 --> 00:06:46,804
"There's an old gravel pit," he says,

200
00:06:46,804 --> 00:06:48,722
"east of our fields.

201
00:06:48,722 --> 00:06:50,635
Steep walls on every side.

202
00:06:50,635 --> 00:06:52,436
One road down into it,

203
00:06:52,436 --> 00:06:54,916
and it is the same road out."

204
00:06:54,916 --> 00:06:57,485
From day 250 to day 252,

205
00:06:57,485 --> 00:06:59,619
you go and look at it.

206
00:07:00,041 --> 00:07:01,903
You and Ansel take the truck,

207
00:07:01,903 --> 00:07:03,145
the long way round,

208
00:07:03,145 --> 00:07:06,768
along farm tracks, with the fields white on both sides.

209
00:07:06,768 --> 00:07:07,644
The pit is six

210
00:07:07,644 --> 00:07:09,526
kilometers past the junction.

211
00:07:09,526 --> 00:07:11,922
You hear it before you see it,

212
00:07:11,922 --> 00:07:13,845
because there is nothing to hear.

213
00:07:13,845 --> 00:07:14,885
Just wind,

214
00:07:14,885 --> 00:07:18,137
going around and around inside a hole in the ground.

215
00:07:18,608 --> 00:07:19,546
It is huge.

216
00:07:19,546 --> 00:07:22,656
A great grey bowl dug into the earth,

217
00:07:22,656 --> 00:07:23,563
with walls as steep

218
00:07:23,563 --> 00:07:25,359
as a staircase stood on its end.

219
00:07:26,053 --> 00:07:26,958
At the bottom,

220
00:07:26,958 --> 00:07:29,370
a frozen puddle the size of a car park.

221
00:07:29,370 --> 00:07:31,707
And one road, curving down along the

222
00:07:31,707 --> 00:07:34,774
inside of the wall, all the way to the bottom.

223
00:07:34,774 --> 00:07:36,554
You stand on the rim for a long time.

224
00:07:36,554 --> 00:07:38,155
You know what the dead do.

225
00:07:38,155 --> 00:07:39,950
They walk toward a sound.

226
00:07:39,950 --> 00:07:41,975
They stop where it stops.

227
00:07:41,975 --> 00:07:43,778
And they do not climb.

228
00:07:43,778 --> 00:07:44,820
On day 251,

229
00:07:44,820 --> 00:07:47,561
you bring Nora and Vera to see it.

230
00:07:47,934 --> 00:07:49,390
Nora looks down into the pit,

231
00:07:49,390 --> 00:07:52,058
then along the single road curving down into it.

232
00:07:52,058 --> 00:07:55,004
"A place with one way out," she says.

233
00:07:55,620 --> 00:07:58,578
"My favorite kind," says Vera.

234
00:07:58,578 --> 00:08:01,805
On day 252, you count everything twice.

235
00:08:01,805 --> 00:08:02,942
The coach's tank.

236
00:08:02,942 --> 00:08:04,218
The truck's tank.

237
00:08:04,218 --> 00:08:05,002
The rope.

238
00:08:05,002 --> 00:08:06,257
The jump leads.

239
00:08:06,257 --> 00:08:08,210
The tape, which Wes keeps in

240
00:08:08,210 --> 00:08:08,992
his pocket now,

241
00:08:08,992 --> 00:08:11,378
in case anything else needs a promise kept.

242
00:08:11,378 --> 00:08:14,891
On day 253, you take the motorway apart.

243
00:08:15,314 --> 00:08:16,312
Not all of it.

244
00:08:16,312 --> 00:08:18,175
Just four sections of the long

245
00:08:18,175 --> 00:08:20,273
metal barrier down the middle,

246
00:08:20,273 --> 00:08:22,462
the bent ones, the ones that leaned

247
00:08:22,462 --> 00:08:25,415
toward you on day 215 with a few

248
00:08:25,415 --> 00:08:28,201
thousand people pressing against them.

249
00:08:28,201 --> 00:08:30,456
Ansel's people bring spanners.

250
00:08:30,456 --> 00:08:32,372
The bolts are rusted and

251
00:08:32,372 --> 00:08:35,245
stubborn and squeal like gulls.

252
00:08:35,245 --> 00:08:37,985
By dark, four sections of barrier

253
00:08:37,985 --> 00:08:40,257
lie in the back of the white truck.

254
00:08:40,257 --> 00:08:41,811
A waist-high barrier is

255
00:08:41,811 --> 00:08:43,570
as good as a wall to them.

256
00:08:43,570 --> 00:08:45,952
You found that out the hard way.

257
00:08:45,952 --> 00:08:48,624
Now you are going to use it the easy way.

258
00:08:48,624 --> 00:08:50,646
That night, everybody takes their place.

259
00:08:50,646 --> 00:08:52,277
Vera will drive the coach.

260
00:08:52,635 --> 00:08:54,512
Wes will ride with her, with the tape.

261
00:08:54,512 --> 00:08:56,964
You will watch them come off the bridge,

262
00:08:56,964 --> 00:08:58,690
then drive the truck with the barrier

263
00:08:58,690 --> 00:09:00,780
the long way round, and wait out of

264
00:09:00,780 --> 00:09:03,187
sight near the top of the road into the pit.

265
00:09:03,561 --> 00:09:04,819
Nora will be on the rim,

266
00:09:04,819 --> 00:09:06,829
with the flashlight, and the rope.

267
00:09:07,315 --> 00:09:08,752
Ansel's people will be

268
00:09:08,752 --> 00:09:10,188
on the rim beside her.

269
00:09:10,188 --> 00:09:11,773
"The rule," says Nora,

270
00:09:11,773 --> 00:09:13,331
on the motorway, in the dark.

271
00:09:13,331 --> 00:09:15,064
"If they come toward the gate,

272
00:09:15,064 --> 00:09:16,456
you close it," you say.

273
00:09:16,456 --> 00:09:18,632
"There isn't a gate," says Nora.

274
00:09:19,135 --> 00:09:21,947
"Then we'll have to build one," says Vera.

275
00:09:21,947 --> 00:09:23,664
On day 254, at first light,

276
00:09:23,664 --> 00:09:25,894
Vera drives the coach up to the junction.

277
00:09:25,894 --> 00:09:27,947
From where you wait with the truck,

278
00:09:27,947 --> 00:09:29,195
far down a farm track,

279
00:09:29,195 --> 00:09:31,644
you can only see the top of the bridge.

280
00:09:31,644 --> 00:09:32,704
It is still black from

281
00:09:32,704 --> 00:09:34,013
one railing to the other.

282
00:09:34,013 --> 00:09:35,445
A month of standing has

283
00:09:35,445 --> 00:09:37,419
not moved one of them an inch.

284
00:09:37,419 --> 00:09:39,024
They are facing nowhere,

285
00:09:39,024 --> 00:09:40,608
waiting for a horn.

286
00:09:40,982 --> 00:09:42,605
Then the horn comes.

287
00:09:42,605 --> 00:09:43,455
Not short.

288
00:09:43,455 --> 00:09:44,219
Long.

289
00:09:44,753 --> 00:09:46,657
The one that empties a flyover.

290
00:09:46,657 --> 00:09:48,650
It rolls up the slip road and

291
00:09:48,650 --> 00:09:50,552
over the bridge, and the whole black

292
00:09:50,552 --> 00:09:52,416
line on top of it turns at once,

293
00:09:52,416 --> 00:09:54,682
like a field of wheat in the wind.

294
00:09:55,185 --> 00:09:57,455
They come down off the bridge.

295
00:09:57,455 --> 00:09:58,341
Slowly.

296
00:09:58,940 --> 00:09:59,953
Then all of them.

297
00:09:59,953 --> 00:10:01,980
They pour down the slip road toward

298
00:10:01,980 --> 00:10:04,428
the coach like sand out of a bag,

299
00:10:04,428 --> 00:10:06,171
and Vera lets them get close,

300
00:10:06,171 --> 00:10:08,075
closer than you would ever dare,

301
00:10:08,075 --> 00:10:11,020
until their hands are almost on the back windows.

302
00:10:11,538 --> 00:10:13,312
Then she pulls away at the speed

303
00:10:13,312 --> 00:10:14,495
of a very slow queue,

304
00:10:14,495 --> 00:10:17,387
and you turn the truck around and take the long

305
00:10:17,387 --> 00:10:18,171
way to the pit,

306
00:10:18,171 --> 00:10:21,355
fast, with four sections of barrier rattling in the back.

307
00:10:21,355 --> 00:10:22,825
It takes all day.

308
00:10:22,825 --> 00:10:24,372
The coach crawls along the farm

309
00:10:24,372 --> 00:10:26,404
road with the river walking behind it,

310
00:10:26,404 --> 00:10:27,871
six kilometers of the dead

311
00:10:27,871 --> 00:10:30,167
strung out between frozen fields.

312
00:10:30,556 --> 00:10:32,282
Every few minutes, the horn.

313
00:10:32,282 --> 00:10:33,413
Every few minutes,

314
00:10:33,413 --> 00:10:35,693
a few thousand heads lift toward it.

315
00:10:35,693 --> 00:10:37,110
On the rim of the pit,

316
00:10:37,110 --> 00:10:39,424
Nora watches them come over the fields,

317
00:10:39,424 --> 00:10:41,405
and flashes the light once.

318
00:10:41,405 --> 00:10:42,307
Still coming.

319
00:10:42,307 --> 00:10:43,144
All of them.

320
00:10:43,144 --> 00:10:45,074
Late in the afternoon,

321
00:10:45,074 --> 00:10:48,432
the coach reaches the pit, and starts down the road into it.

322
00:10:48,432 --> 00:10:49,772
Down along the wall.

323
00:10:49,772 --> 00:10:51,364
Around the long curve.

324
00:10:51,364 --> 00:10:53,649
Halfway down, on a patch of ice,

325
00:10:53,649 --> 00:10:56,612
the back of the coach slides toward the edge,

326
00:10:56,612 --> 00:10:58,027
and from the rim you see

327
00:10:58,027 --> 00:11:00,153
Vera's arms turn the big wheel,

328
00:11:00,153 --> 00:11:03,193
slowly, with two fingers, like a teacup.

329
00:11:03,743 --> 00:11:04,747
The wheels grip.

330
00:11:04,747 --> 00:11:06,045
Nora breathes out for

331
00:11:06,045 --> 00:11:08,152
the first time in a minute.

332
00:11:08,152 --> 00:11:10,110
Then on, all the way to the bottom,

333
00:11:10,110 --> 00:11:12,645
where it stops beside the frozen puddle.

334
00:11:12,645 --> 00:11:14,863
Behind it, the river comes over

335
00:11:14,863 --> 00:11:16,844
the edge and starts down the road,

336
00:11:16,844 --> 00:11:18,950
a dark ribbon winding into the bowl.

337
00:11:18,950 --> 00:11:19,903
Inside the coach,

338
00:11:19,903 --> 00:11:23,507
Wes leans over the wheel and tapes the horn down.

339
00:11:23,507 --> 00:11:24,173
Neatly.

340
00:11:24,173 --> 00:11:25,257
Very neatly.

341
00:11:25,257 --> 00:11:27,301
The horn goes on and on,

342
00:11:27,301 --> 00:11:30,032
filling the whole pit like water filling a sink.

343
00:11:30,422 --> 00:11:31,502
Through the back window,

344
00:11:31,502 --> 00:11:34,900
the road behind them is already full of faces, coming down.

345
00:11:34,900 --> 00:11:35,823
Not angry.

346
00:11:35,823 --> 00:11:37,129
Not hungry.

347
00:11:37,567 --> 00:11:38,525
Just listening,

348
00:11:38,525 --> 00:11:40,501
the way they always listen.

349
00:11:41,260 --> 00:11:43,003
Then the roof hatch opens.

350
00:11:43,003 --> 00:11:46,192
Vera climbs out first, and Wes after her.

351
00:11:46,192 --> 00:11:47,138
Second door.

352
00:11:47,138 --> 00:11:49,922
From the rim, Nora throws down the rope.

353
00:11:49,922 --> 00:11:51,925
It unrolls down the steep wall and

354
00:11:51,925 --> 00:11:54,576
lands beside the coach, and Vera ties it

355
00:11:54,576 --> 00:11:56,785
under her arms without hurrying once.

356
00:11:57,238 --> 00:11:58,621
"Pull," says Nora.

357
00:11:58,621 --> 00:11:59,434
You pull.

358
00:11:59,434 --> 00:12:00,792
Ansel pulls.

359
00:12:01,149 --> 00:12:02,220
Everybody pulls.

360
00:12:02,220 --> 00:12:05,173
Vera comes up the wall hand over hand,

361
00:12:05,173 --> 00:12:06,920
and then Wes, as the first of the

362
00:12:06,920 --> 00:12:08,985
dead reach the bottom of the road and

363
00:12:08,985 --> 00:12:10,945
flow out across the floor of the pit,

364
00:12:10,945 --> 00:12:13,383
around the coach, toward the sound.

365
00:12:13,383 --> 00:12:15,274
They keep coming until dusk.

366
00:12:15,274 --> 00:12:16,544
Thousands of them,

367
00:12:16,544 --> 00:12:18,432
down one road, into one bowl,

368
00:12:18,432 --> 00:12:21,354
the way they came into your yard on day one.

369
00:12:21,354 --> 00:12:23,460
And the last two down the road,

370
00:12:23,460 --> 00:12:26,157
walking slowly, side by side,

371
00:12:26,157 --> 00:12:28,829
wear a blue depot vest and an olive one.

372
00:12:29,283 --> 00:12:30,471
The night driver.

373
00:12:30,471 --> 00:12:31,593
And the Doorman,

374
00:12:31,593 --> 00:12:36,252
one step behind him, the way he has been since day 190.

375
00:12:36,737 --> 00:12:38,949
Nora stands at the very edge of the rim.

376
00:12:38,949 --> 00:12:41,112
She doesn't say anything this time.

377
00:12:41,112 --> 00:12:42,620
She doesn't need to.

378
00:12:42,620 --> 00:12:45,480
"It was a good bus," Vera tells him,

379
00:12:45,480 --> 00:12:47,049
quietly, from up there.

380
00:12:47,049 --> 00:12:48,134
"I told you."

381
00:12:48,620 --> 00:12:49,590
Then you drive the

382
00:12:49,590 --> 00:12:51,120
truck to the top of the road.

383
00:12:51,120 --> 00:12:52,534
Everybody lifts.

384
00:12:52,534 --> 00:12:53,726
Ansel's people,

385
00:12:53,726 --> 00:12:56,555
the girl, Wes, Vera, you.

386
00:12:56,555 --> 00:12:59,885
Four sections of motorway barrier go

387
00:12:59,885 --> 00:13:01,564
across the top of the road,

388
00:13:01,564 --> 00:13:05,299
bolted end to end, waist-high, from wall to wall.

389
00:13:05,299 --> 00:13:07,390
It is the first gate you have ever

390
00:13:07,390 --> 00:13:09,727
closed with everyone on the right side of it.

391
00:13:09,727 --> 00:13:11,785
That night, the horn stops.

392
00:13:11,785 --> 00:13:13,459
The battery is done.

393
00:13:13,960 --> 00:13:14,814
Down in the pit,

394
00:13:14,814 --> 00:13:17,968
the river stands exactly where the last sound was,

395
00:13:17,968 --> 00:13:19,826
in the dark, facing a bus,

396
00:13:19,826 --> 00:13:24,990
waiting for a horn that is never going to blast again.

397
00:13:24,990 --> 00:13:27,372
From day 255 to day 258,

398
00:13:27,372 --> 00:13:30,499
the bridge belongs to the living.

399
00:13:30,952 --> 00:13:32,124
On day 255,

400
00:13:32,124 --> 00:13:35,822
Ansel's people walk across it in broad daylight,

401
00:13:35,822 --> 00:13:37,538
with buckets, toward the spring.

402
00:13:38,073 --> 00:13:39,145
Nobody whispers.

403
00:13:39,145 --> 00:13:41,967
One of them starts to sing, very badly.

404
00:13:42,357 --> 00:13:44,018
Nobody tells him to stop.

405
00:13:44,018 --> 00:13:46,634
You stand on the bridge with Nora,

406
00:13:46,634 --> 00:13:48,170
at the top of the slip road,

407
00:13:48,170 --> 00:13:50,443
where a month ago you leaned on a

408
00:13:50,443 --> 00:13:52,000
horn and rolled away in silence.

409
00:13:52,000 --> 00:13:53,931
There is nothing on it now but frost,

410
00:13:53,931 --> 00:13:54,928
and footprints,

411
00:13:54,928 --> 00:13:59,059
and a girl pulling an empty handcart, running.

412
00:13:59,059 --> 00:14:02,433
On day 256, Ansel shows you the city.

413
00:14:02,433 --> 00:14:03,874
Just the edge of it.

414
00:14:04,313 --> 00:14:05,447
Empty streets.

415
00:14:05,447 --> 00:14:06,506
Shut windows.

416
00:14:06,506 --> 00:14:08,827
And a tall, narrow house on a corner,

417
00:14:08,827 --> 00:14:10,818
with a lamp in the top window,

418
00:14:10,818 --> 00:14:12,819
unlit now, because nobody needs to be

419
00:14:12,819 --> 00:14:15,272
told anymore that somebody has seen them.

420
00:14:15,272 --> 00:14:16,759
There are nineteen of them.

421
00:14:16,759 --> 00:14:18,624
They live upstairs,

422
00:14:18,624 --> 00:14:20,405
the way you lived downstairs.

423
00:14:20,405 --> 00:14:23,054
"You could stay," Ansel tells Vera.

424
00:14:23,054 --> 00:14:24,610
"We could use a driver."

425
00:14:24,610 --> 00:14:26,790
Vera looks out at the motorway,

426
00:14:26,790 --> 00:14:27,548
toward the town,

427
00:14:27,548 --> 00:14:30,276
toward the hill and a depot you can't see from here.

428
00:14:30,276 --> 00:14:31,679
"I've got a place with

429
00:14:31,679 --> 00:14:33,660
one way out," she says.

430
00:14:33,660 --> 00:14:35,148
"But thank you."

431
00:14:35,148 --> 00:14:36,418
On day 258,

432
00:14:36,418 --> 00:14:39,655
before you leave, Ansel gives Nora a road map,

433
00:14:39,655 --> 00:14:41,895
soft and folded a hundred times.

434
00:14:41,895 --> 00:14:44,755
On it, in pencil, there is a circle

435
00:14:44,755 --> 00:14:46,955
around a place at the edge of the paper.

436
00:14:46,955 --> 00:14:47,791
Blue sea.

437
00:14:48,196 --> 00:14:50,671
Two days' drive, when the roads are clear.

438
00:14:50,671 --> 00:14:53,254
Wes looks over her shoulder.

439
00:14:53,254 --> 00:14:55,781
"That's the beach," he says.

440
00:14:55,781 --> 00:14:58,396
From day 259 to day 262,

441
00:14:58,396 --> 00:15:02,110
you drive home with full tanks.

442
00:15:02,110 --> 00:15:05,396
On day 262, you stop at your own gate,

443
00:15:05,396 --> 00:15:07,729
and before anybody in the cab can move,

444
00:15:08,103 --> 00:15:10,493
there is a knock from the inside.

445
00:15:10,493 --> 00:15:11,125
Three times.

446
00:15:11,125 --> 00:15:13,466
Then a fourth time, softer.

447
00:15:13,466 --> 00:15:14,966
The bolt lifts.

448
00:15:15,324 --> 00:15:16,655
The gate whispers open.

449
00:15:16,655 --> 00:15:19,086
And there is the boy with the blue bandage,

450
00:15:19,086 --> 00:15:20,293
holding the flashlight

451
00:15:20,293 --> 00:15:23,389
like a promise, very proud of himself.

452
00:15:23,389 --> 00:15:26,544
That evening, Wes takes the pencil and

453
00:15:26,544 --> 00:15:28,897
adds nineteen marks to the people met column.

454
00:15:29,272 --> 00:15:30,424
One at a time.

455
00:15:30,424 --> 00:15:31,723
Very slowly.

456
00:15:32,097 --> 00:15:35,250
Enjoying every single one.

457
00:15:35,250 --> 00:15:38,729
From day 263 to day 269,

458
00:15:38,729 --> 00:15:41,033
the depot rests.

459
00:15:41,472 --> 00:15:44,174
Every sunset, Ansel comes on the radio.

460
00:15:44,174 --> 00:15:45,421
"Pit's quiet.

461
00:15:45,421 --> 00:15:46,599
Bridge is ours."

462
00:15:46,599 --> 00:15:49,963
Every sunset, Nora says, "Still here."

463
00:15:49,963 --> 00:15:52,081
Wes oils the gate.

464
00:15:52,081 --> 00:15:53,671
Vera sleeps sitting up,

465
00:15:53,671 --> 00:15:54,996
with the door open.

466
00:15:54,996 --> 00:15:57,571
Nora pins the road map inside the open locker,

467
00:15:57,571 --> 00:15:59,649
next to the postcard of the beach.

468
00:16:00,022 --> 00:16:01,341
The loudspeaker switch

469
00:16:01,341 --> 00:16:02,660
is still taped on OFF.

470
00:16:02,660 --> 00:16:05,001
Most mornings, the truck still goes out,

471
00:16:05,001 --> 00:16:07,306
one short blast at every corner,

472
00:16:07,306 --> 00:16:09,185
but there is less and less to lead.

473
00:16:09,185 --> 00:16:11,734
Some mornings there is nothing at all,

474
00:16:11,734 --> 00:16:13,228
and you just drive around the lower

475
00:16:13,228 --> 00:16:15,869
town with the window down, because you can.

476
00:16:15,869 --> 00:16:17,121
On day 266,

477
00:16:17,121 --> 00:16:20,153
Vera sits down next to you on the bench and

478
00:16:20,153 --> 00:16:22,037
puts her goggles in your hands.

479
00:16:22,556 --> 00:16:23,808
"You drove that slip road

480
00:16:23,808 --> 00:16:25,704
with two fingers," she says.

481
00:16:25,704 --> 00:16:26,317
"Keep them.

482
00:16:26,317 --> 00:16:27,820
I know I'm still here now.

483
00:16:27,820 --> 00:16:29,971
I don't need anything to remind me."

484
00:16:29,971 --> 00:16:32,209
You don't know what to say.

485
00:16:32,209 --> 00:16:34,116
So you put them in the orange bag,

486
00:16:34,116 --> 00:16:35,485
very carefully,

487
00:16:35,485 --> 00:16:37,811
next to everything else you are keeping.

488
00:16:37,811 --> 00:16:39,385
Wes says that bag is going

489
00:16:39,385 --> 00:16:41,077
to need its own bunker soon.

490
00:16:41,077 --> 00:16:43,042
Nora says it already has one.

491
00:16:43,042 --> 00:16:44,690
Nora adds a mark to days

492
00:16:44,690 --> 00:16:46,770
in daylight every evening.

493
00:16:47,224 --> 00:16:48,380
By day 269,

494
00:16:48,380 --> 00:16:52,325
the column is longer than any column on

495
00:16:52,325 --> 00:16:54,608
the wall except the days.

496
00:16:54,608 --> 00:16:58,189
On day 270, the night is clear and quiet.

497
00:16:58,189 --> 00:17:01,075
The four of you go down to the bunker,

498
00:17:01,075 --> 00:17:02,474
the way you always do,

499
00:17:02,474 --> 00:17:04,974
and Nora turns the lantern down low.

500
00:17:04,974 --> 00:17:07,323
Then, through the vent grille

501
00:17:07,323 --> 00:17:09,857
above your heads, you hear footsteps.

502
00:17:09,857 --> 00:17:11,095
Not shuffling.

503
00:17:11,614 --> 00:17:13,095
Not dragging.

504
00:17:13,095 --> 00:17:13,836
Boots.

505
00:17:13,836 --> 00:17:15,511
Living ones.

506
00:17:16,287 --> 00:17:17,199
Several of them,

507
00:17:17,199 --> 00:17:21,060
crossing the street toward the depot, and stopping at the gate.

508
00:17:21,060 --> 00:17:22,402
A thin line of torchlight

509
00:17:22,402 --> 00:17:24,138
slides across the yard,

510
00:17:24,138 --> 00:17:26,055
finds the grille, and stops there,

511
00:17:26,055 --> 00:17:29,053
as if somebody knows exactly where to look.

512
00:17:29,053 --> 00:17:30,189
You hold your breath.

513
00:17:30,189 --> 00:17:31,942
The others hold theirs.

514
00:17:31,942 --> 00:17:34,053
And somebody knocks.

515
00:17:34,053 --> 00:17:34,757
Twice.

516
00:17:34,757 --> 00:17:35,660
Hard.

517
00:17:36,114 --> 00:17:37,017
Then nothing.

518
00:17:37,017 --> 00:17:39,511
Nobody you know knocks like that.

519
00:17:39,950 --> 00:17:40,936
Two hundred and seventy days.

520
00:17:40,936 --> 00:17:43,700
The same orange bandage.

521
00:17:44,154 --> 00:17:46,269
Nora is holding the flashlight.

522
00:17:46,269 --> 00:17:48,678
You are holding the orange bag.

523
00:17:48,678 --> 00:17:51,531
Tomorrow is day 271.

524
00:17:52,002 --> 00:17:54,405
The river is in a pit with a gate across it,

525
00:17:54,405 --> 00:17:56,333
the bridge belongs to the living,

526
00:17:56,333 --> 00:18:00,438
and the sign over the street says FOUR ALIVE.

527
00:18:00,438 --> 00:18:03,026
For two hundred and seventy days,

528
00:18:03,384 --> 00:18:04,506
you have known exactly

529
00:18:04,506 --> 00:18:06,367
how the dead come to your door.

530
00:18:06,935 --> 00:18:08,816
Tonight, for the first time,

531
00:18:08,816 --> 00:18:11,490
you don't know who the living are.

532
00:18:11,490 --> 00:18:13,762
Would you have gone back for the river?

533
00:18:13,762 --> 00:18:15,041
Which decision would

534
00:18:15,041 --> 00:18:16,529
you have made differently?

535
00:18:16,529 --> 00:18:17,906
Tell us in the comments,

536
00:18:17,906 --> 00:18:20,541
and subscribe to Last Safe Door,

537
00:18:20,541 --> 00:18:22,950
so you're here for day 271.
